     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello<div><br></div><div>Below is a simple reproducible app.  I have two tabs. Tab 1 displays a chart while Tab 2 displays a chart and table.</div><div><br></div><div>I have also a download button in the side bar and an Rmd document.</div><div><br></div><div>The question is, the resulting html page I want to download fails unless I select Tab 2.  When I select Tab 2 the download works fine even if I go back to Tab 1 before downloading. Obviously this is due in part to the reactive element on Tab 2.</div><div><br></div><div>However, I want the download to work whether or not I visit Tab 2.  In other words when the app loads I can just click the download button and the resulting html page will contain the charts and the table from both tabs.</div><div><br></div><div>Is there a way to preload Tab 2?  As you can see, I have tried the outputOptions function with suspendWhenHidden = FALSE but it doesn&#39;t seen to work.</div><div><br></div><div>Any help please?</div><div><br></div><div><b>Shiny</b></div><div><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\">library</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\">shiny</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>library</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\">rmarkdown</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br><br><br>data</span><span style=\"font-family: